1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,232
One billion pixels. One single planet.

2
00:00:06,132 --> 00:00:10,846
Imagine the world map split into one billion tiny squares.

3
00:00:11,496 --> 00:00:15,850
Each of those squares can belong to exactly one person.

4
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:22,392
You pick a free spot: your street, your favorite place, or somewhere out in the ocean.

5
00:00:23,042 --> 00:00:30,372
One euro. Paid once, yours forever. No subscription, no rent.

6
00:00:31,072 --> 00:00:35,378
You also get a certificate with your name and your pixel number.

7
00:00:36,028 --> 00:00:41,078
On the map you can see who is where, and which country is currently ahead.

8
00:00:41,728 --> 00:00:48,434
Right now, almost the whole map is still free. Your spot has not been taken yet.

9
00:00:49,284 --> 00:00:52,942
Claim your pixel at pixelmaps.org.
